    q: "What are Planned Value (PV), Earned Value (EV), and Actual Cost (AC) in Earned Value Management?",
    a: "Planned Value is the authorized, budgeted cost of the work that WAS SCHEDULED to be done by a given point in time (read from the cost baseline). Earned Value is the budgeted cost of the work ACTUALLY COMPLETED by that point — it converts physical progress into a dollar figure comparable to PV and AC, which is EVM's core trick. Actual Cost is what was REALLY SPENT to achieve that completed work. All three are needed together because any one alone is misleading: spending a lot (high AC) tells you nothing about whether that spend produced proportional progress (EV) or whether it was even on the schedule you'd planned (PV).",
