    q: "What is the Cost Performance Index (CPI), and how do you interpret it?",
    a: "CPI = EV / AC — it measures cost efficiency: how much value you're earning per dollar actually spent. CPI = 1.0 means spending exactly as budgeted for the work done; CPI < 1.0 means over budget (you're spending more than the value of work completed — e.g. CPI = 0.8 means you're only getting 80 cents of earned value per dollar spent); CPI > 1.0 means under budget (getting more value per dollar than planned). CPI is widely considered a strong, stable predictor of final cost performance even fairly early in a project's execution, which is exactly why it's central to EAC forecasting.",
