    a: "Avoid — eliminate the threat entirely, usually by changing the plan (removing the risky activity, choosing a different, safer approach). Mitigate — reduce the probability and/or impact to an acceptable level (adding redundancy, extra testing, simpler design) without eliminating the risk entirely. Transfer — shift the financial/ownership impact to a third party (insurance, a fixed-price contract that puts cost-overrun risk on the seller, a warranty) — note this transfers financial impact, not necessarily the underlying risk of the event itself happening. Accept — consciously decide not to change the plan in response, either passively (do nothing beyond noting it) or actively (set aside a contingency reserve in case it happens) — appropriate when the cost of responding exceeds the risk's expected impact.",
